    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the knowledge of the truth which is according to godliness, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "in hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before times eternal; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but in his own seasons manifested his word in the message, wherewith I was intrusted according to the commandment of God our Saviour; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "to Titus, my true child after a common faith: Grace and peace from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Saviour.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that were wanting, and appoint elders in every city, as I gave thee charge; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "if any man is blameless, the husband of one wife, having children that believe, who are not accused of riot or unruly. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the bishop must be blameless, as God’s steward; not self-willed, not soon angry, no brawler, no striker, not greedy of filthy lucre; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "but given to hospitality, a lover of good, sober-minded, just, holy, self-controlled; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "holding to the faithful word which is according to the teaching, that he may be able both to exhort in the sound doctrine, and to convict the gainsayers.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For there are many unruly men, vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "whose mouths must be stopped; men who overthrow whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "TIT 1:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One of themselves, a prophet of their own, said,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "TIT.1.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "TIT.1.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
